WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.334
A clean ablation over subgraph order tells the
story on real data.

00:00:04.414 --> 00:00:06.876
Using only single edges, at order one,

00:00:06.956 --> 00:00:11.959
neither test can separate the density-matched
networks, exactly as expected.

00:00:12.039 --> 00:00:16.842
Adding two-edge subgraphs already tips the balance
in favor of cumulants.

00:00:16.922 --> 00:00:21.323
Adding three-edge subgraphs pushes the cumulant
test further ahead,

00:00:21.403 --> 00:00:25.202
while the moment test starts to overfit and slip backward.

00:00:25.282 --> 00:00:30.954
Sweeping the block-model parameters and the sample
size confirms this advantage is not

00:00:31.034 --> 00:00:33.362
a quirk of one setting but a robust,

00:00:33.442 --> 00:00:34.700
qualitative feature.
